{
  "name": "nav-det (app chrome: sidebar nav + topbar + user menu + command palette, operator + builder, builder-cluster gating asserted)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against components/app/{Sidebar,Topbar,UserMenu}.svelte + ui/command/{Command,CommandItem}.svelte + keyboard/globalShortcuts.ts.",
    "Builder cluster (nav-llm, nav-transcriptions, sidebar-builder-separator, sidebar-builder-cluster-label) renders only when uiMode === 'builder' (Sidebar.svelte {#if isBuilder}). In operator mode it is asserted ABSENT via waitGone.",
    "Command palette items carry interpolated ids `command-item-{action-id}` (CommandItem.svelte); the old exact `command-item` no longer exists, so a generic item is matched via testidPrefix.",
    "topbar-search click dispatches Cmd+K, which globalShortcuts.ts TOGGLES; a second click closes the palette.",
    "user-menu-about navigates to the About settings sub-page (UserMenu.goAbout -> navigateToSettings('about')); there is no About dialog, so the landing is asserted on about-section and there is nothing to close.",
    "topbar-agents-at-work renders only when running tasks > 0 (data-dependent) and is observed by screenshot only, never hard-asserted. topbar-sidebar-toggle renders only when sidebarState === 'drawer' (Topbar.svelte:33), i.e. under 768 px (layout.ts:28-36, 116-123), and is reached by the narrow block below.",
    "Narrow block: resizeWindow 700x800 (the runner lifts the 900x600 minimum of tauri.conf.json, then restores it) puts the viewport under the 768 px md query, so sidebarState becomes 'drawer' and topbar-sidebar-toggle renders; its click is layoutActions.openDrawer (Topbar.svelte:37, layout.ts:169-171), which mounts sidebar-drawer-backdrop (Sidebar.svelte:122-133), whose click is closeDrawer (:130). The block contains no picker and no window.confirm, closes the drawer before resizing back, and ends on resizeWindow 1280x800 plus a waitGone of the toggle, so every later section sees the wide chrome. The drawer state persisted under apollia.ui.sidebarState_sm (layout.ts:105-110) is in the runner's boot reset list.",
    "runtime-disconnected-retry is reached by the fault step heartbeat-lost: the runtime heartbeat is an event the backend emits every five seconds and no IPC can silence, so the dev-only hook mutes the liveness listeners and fires the watchdog. The retry unmutes them, and the next real heartbeat closes the banner, which the waitGone asserts."
  ],
